# Insurance Claims SQL Analysis

This project simulates an insurance claims database and includes sample SQL queries to analyze customer claim behavior.

## 🧮 What It Does

- Creates two related tables: `Customers` and `Claims`
- Inserts sample data for multiple customers and claims
- Includes queries to:
  - Total claims per customer
  - Average claim by risk category
  - Filter claims by age and amount
  - Identify the largest claim

## 🛠 Tech Used

- SQL (PostgreSQL syntax, portable to others)
- Joins, GROUP BY, HAVING, ORDER BY, and filtering
- Query logic saved in `.sql` format

## 📌 Why This Exists

Built as a real-world modeling project to strengthen data analysis and relational database skills relevant to actuarial and insurance analytics.

## 🗂 Files

- `create_tables.sql`: Table definitions for Customers and Claims
- `insert_data.sql`: Sample data
- `queries.sql`: A set of useful reporting queries
